WEBVTT

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:04.280
Now I can summon monsters between 
Level 4 and 10 simultaneously!

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.000
Pendulum Summon!

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:10.150
The elder ghost clad in strong winds,

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:15.710
remove your wild garments to create a 
large river and hollow out the land!

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:19.770
Come out, Mayosenju Daibak!

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.340
I'll finish our fight!

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.970
Finish?  Don't be silly.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.140
The duel has only just begun!

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.740
What?

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.380
The fun is only getting started!

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:40.890
Implementing mass into Solid 
Vision has created Action Duels.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:46.030
In duels where the field, monsters 
and duelists become one,

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:49.090
the people are caught in 
a frenzy of excitement!

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:53.360
Let's start!  From an instant flash

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:56.090
Let's find!  Yeah, the way I ought to go

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:58.760
Let's start!  The fun is only getting started

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:01.590
Ready go!  The real beginning

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:12.680
A future filled with hope 
and anxiety now begins

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:18.150
Don't worry because you have firm desires

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:23.780
I fight to reach the day that I yearn for

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:27.890
The gleaming strength resides inside the card

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:31.830
Repeating Up/Down

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:34.190
Feel It!  The heartbeat Bu,Bu,Bu,Burn!

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:41.440
I become stronger by overcoming 
and shaking off limitations again

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:44.900
Because I don't want to give up

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:49.880
Ride the accelerating wind and head towards

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:56.980
My dream that makes me love tomorrow

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:07.490
Break through those clouds and draw 
your dazzling dreams in the blue sky

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:10.170
Let's start!  From an instant flash

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:12.870
Let's find!  Yeah, the way I ought to go

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:15.670
Let's start!  The fun is only getting started

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:18.440
Ready go!  The real beginning

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:27.990
Fierce Battle!  Entertainment Duel Show!!

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:38.100
Amazing!  Such stunning developments!

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.200
It was rumored that only Sakaki 
could use Pendulum Summon.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:45.080
But Sawatari was able to use it!

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:51.480
And his Yosen Lost Tornado combo sealed away 
all of Sakaki's Pendulum Cards in his deck.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.320
Sakaki has zero cards in his hand.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:55.950
What can he do?

00:02:56.350 --> 00:03:00.400
I only came to see Pendulum Summon, 
but this duel is incredible!

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.200
I can't believe they both used Pendulum!

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.280
Yuya, it all begins now!

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.900
Open the path with your own power!

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.280
Yuya!

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:10.640
Do your best!

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:17.310
I applaud you for still having 
hope in an Action Card.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:20.400
But all you have is despair.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.310
My turn!

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:27.050
I summon Yosenju Kama 1 from my hand!

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:34.450
Since I successfully summoned 
Kama 1, I summon Yosenju Kama 2!

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:40.600
Then due to Kama 2's effect, 
I summon Yosenju Kama 3!

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:44.780
The Continuous Spell Yosen Training 
Grounds's effect also activates!

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:47.820
For every Yosenju that is 
summoned or Special Summoned,

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:50.210
one Yosen Counter lights up.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:55.650
While you were searching for an Action 
Card, I finished my preparations.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.200
Now's the time to end it.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.230
Okay!

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:19.300
I know your plan.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:25.650
You're trying to distract me from your 
two set cards, but that won't happen.

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:29.850
Kama 1's effect can't 
return a set card, but...

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:33.100
I activate Yosenju Shinchu 
R's Pendulum effect!

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:37.240
When there's a Yosenju in 
the other Pendulum Zone,

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:41.160
the Pendulum Scale changes from 5 
to 11 until the end of the turn!

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:45.260
Now I can summon monsters between 
Level 4 and 10 simultaneously!

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:50.270
Pendulum Summon!

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:54.770
The elder ghost clad in strong winds,

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:59.850
remove your wild garments to create a 
large river and hollow out the land!

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:04.450
Come out, Mayosenju Daibak!

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.190
One Yosen Counter lights up.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.390
Yuya, what are you going to do?

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:17.100
Daibak's effect also works on set cards!

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:20.130
He's trying to get rid of Yuya's cards!

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:22.370
Daibak's effect activates!

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:25.340
Two cards on the field return to the hand!

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:31.640
I also activate Dizzying Winds 
of Yosen Village's effect

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:34.620
to return those two cards to your deck.

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:36.110
This is the end.

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:41.320
Too bad!  You went through the trouble of 
setting those cards, but it was a waste!

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:46.920
No, it's fine!

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:57.840
When this set card leaves the field, all 
your monsters become nameless this turn!

00:05:58.420 --> 00:05:59.350
What?

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:04.880
Whoa!  Sawatari's monsters lost their names!

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:08.140
You were planning this from the start!

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:09.780
That's right!

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:13.750
Dizzying Winds of Yosen Village's 
effect doesn't affect Yosenjus.

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:14.320
However...

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:15.520
I see!

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:20.840
Since Sawatari's monsters are no longer 
Yosenjus, at the end of the turn...

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:23.130
Due to Dizzying Winds of 
Yosen Village's effect,

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:25.930
they return to the deck instead of the hand.

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:31.640
Not bad.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:35.660
I used your card's effect against you.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:40.380
But do you really think you'll 
survive until the end of the turn?

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:44.120
I'll end this duel before then!

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:52.990
Let's battle!

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.600
Daibak attacks you directly!

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:57.700
The others, follow it!

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.170
Sawatari launches an all-out attack!

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:06.040
He's like a warrior attacking 
to take down a castle!

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:10.310
I won't let this end!

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.960
This is the end!

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:18.980
Yuya!

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:27.430
No!

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:29.160
Yuya!

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:30.160
No way...

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:31.750
Yuya...

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:38.640
You lost, Yuya Sakaki.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:46.450
Whoa!  Look over there!

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:48.340
That's...

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:50.180
Yeah!  He did it!

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:52.330
It's Sakaki!

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:53.200
Yuya!

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:54.420
He did it!

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:58.060
No way!  I know the direct attack succeeded!

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:03.400
Did you really think I was running 
around without a plan in mind?

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:06.900
He got an Action Card at 
the last possible second.

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:07.870
Not bad.

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:14.720
He figured out the location of an Action 
Card, and he invited Daibak to attack.

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:19.720
The Action Spell Big Escape!

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:21.750
It forces the battle to end!

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:25.920
Wow!  It's like a magic show!

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:27.390
Nice!

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:33.320
Stop messing around!

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:37.160
You're not the one who's supposed 
to get the crowd excited!

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:39.430
This is my dueling style!

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:43.450
But in the end, the crowd will cheer for me.

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:45.750
Yosen Training Grounds's effect activates!

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:51.550
By using three Yosen Counters, I add 
one Yosenju in my deck to my hand.

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:55.900
I add Kama 3 to my hand and end my turn.

00:08:56.480 --> 00:09:00.520
Now your monsters have to leave.

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:11.550
If a Yosenju doesn't return to 
my hand at the end of my turn,

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:13.830
Yosen Whirlwind is destroyed.

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:17.800
Yosenju Shinchu R's Pendulum 
Scale returns to normal.

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:20.220
Due to Dizzying Winds of 
Yosen Village's effect,

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:25.320
Sawatari's monsters return to 
his deck instead of his hand.

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:29.300
Both our fields look lonely.

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:36.760
I'll make it lively on my next turn when 
your defeat will be the main event!

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:40.560
Sorry, but I don't intend to lose either!

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:46.170
My turn!  I draw!

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:51.360
Good!  When we both don't 
have monsters on our fields,

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:53.710
I can summon this card by 
lowering its Level by 1!

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:57.540
I summon Performapal Drummerilla!

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:04.160
Let's battle!  Drummerilla 
attacks you directly!

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:08.750
So you're attacking me!

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.590
I won't back down!

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:13.290
When you declare a direct attack,

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:20.070
I send one Yosenju in my hand to the 
graveyard to Special Summon Yosenju Oyam!

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:22.380
A Yosen Counter lights up!

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:26.880
Oyam's attack points become the same

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:31.240
as the original attack points of 
the monster it's battling against!

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:33.710
Drummerilla's effect activates!

00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:38.950
One monster gains 600 attack 
points until the end of battle!

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:54.510
Sakaki was in big trouble last turn,

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:57.640
but he's turned things around and 
has dealt damage to Sawatari!

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:02.180
When the battle is over, 
Drummerilla's effect ends!

00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:06.340
All right!  Yuya Sakaki 
is also gaining momentum!

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:08.710
Is he going to Pendulum Summon?

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:10.950
I end my turn.

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:13.420
What?  No Pendulum?

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:14.960
How disappointing.

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.890
Well, he has zero cards in his hand.

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:19.900
Okay okay, don't worry!

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:24.130
I'll successfully and 
beautifully Pendulum Summon!

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:25.860
My turn!

00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:28.410
Due to Yosen Training Grounds's effect,

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:34.410
I use three Yosen Counters to add Mayosenju 
Daibak from my deck to my hand!

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:38.140
Daibak is now in Sawatari's hand!

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:39.320
That means...

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:42.110
Pendulum!  Pendulum!

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:46.120
Pendulum!  Pendulum!

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:49.260
That's right!  Get more excited!

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:52.280
Stronger!  More passionately!

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:54.580
Here I go!

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:58.650
I've already set the 
Pendulum Scale from 3 to 5!

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:02.370
Therefore, I can summon Level 4 monsters!

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:05.520
He's not going to raise 
Yosenju Shinchu R's Scale?

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:07.970
He's not summoning Daibak?

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:09.720
Pendulum Summon!

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:11.710
Appear, the blades that slice the wind!

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:14.210
Yosenju Kama 1!

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:16.260
Kama 3!

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:18.910
Since this counts as a single summoning,

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:22.090
one Yosen Counter lights up 
on Yosen Training Grounds.

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:25.480
I'll get rid of that 
annoying Performapal first.

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:26.790
Kama 1's effect!

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:30.730
I have to get that Action Card!

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:35.770
When there's a non-Kama 1 
Yosen monster on my field,

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:39.140
I can return your monster to your hand once.

00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:41.380
Vanish, Drummerilla!

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:43.340
The Action Spell Invisibility!

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:47.150
My monster isn't affected 
by your effect this turn!

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:48.850
Stop vanishing!

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.600
But you said that you wanted it to vanish!

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:52.950
That's right!

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:56.920
Sakaki managed to survive, but 
his escape path is blocked!

00:12:57.740 --> 00:12:59.630
I still have another strategy!

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:05.720
I tribute Kama 1 and Kama 
3 to Tribute Summon Daibak!

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:15.110
One Yosen Counter lights up.

00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:17.840
Daibak has arrived!

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:20.300
He summoned it without using Pendulum Summon.

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:22.080
He Tribute Summoned.

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:25.740
Why are you smiling?

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:27.650
Don't you know the situation you're in?

00:13:28.060 --> 00:13:32.740
I do, but the crowd is excited.

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:35.740
It's not just me.

00:13:35.740 --> 00:13:38.520
Our back-and-forth battle

00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:42.230
have created an unpredictable 
show that's exciting the crowd!

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:47.580
I didn't know this was possible before, 
so I can't help enjoying this!

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:50.440
I also can't help enjoying this!

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:55.150
Because I can crush you 
in front of a huge crowd!

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:56.840
Sawatari...

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:00.600
I won't let you win so easily!

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:02.590
This show will get even more exciting!

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:05.700
No, now is the climax!

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:07.500
Here I go!  Let's battle!

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:10.200
Daibak attacks Drummerilla!

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:13.500
I activate Drummerilla's effect!

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:19.780
One monster on my field gains 600 
attack points until the end of battle!

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:28.340
The destroyed Drummerilla 
goes to my Extra Deck.

00:14:29.320 --> 00:14:34.590
Sakaki's monster was destroyed, but he 
used its effect to lessen the damage!

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:37.320
Wow!  This really is a hard-fought battle!

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:39.790
Yeah!  It's a great match!

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:45.600
Yuya has grown even more in this duel.

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:48.230
Sawatari is also doing quite well.

00:14:48.640 --> 00:14:50.540
I end my turn.

00:14:50.770 --> 00:14:54.210
Since I Tribute Summoned Daibak, 
it remains on the field.

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:58.640
If he Special Summoned Daibak, it 
would have returned to his hand.

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:02.460
Sawatari Tribute Summoned 
instead to avoid that.

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:06.450
He's using those summoning methods properly.

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:08.690
And he's enjoying himself.

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:12.350
This is Sawatari we're talking about.

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:16.400
Will Yuya Sakaki use Pendulum this time?

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:26.850
Pendulum!  Pendulum!  Pendulum!

00:15:26.850 --> 00:15:29.040
Do it, entertainment duelist.

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:34.850
The stadium is excited about our duel.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:38.050
The crowd is expecting something spectacular!

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:39.750
Sawatari...

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:43.720
It's your turn!  Let's see how you respond!

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:45.850
Okay!

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:50.700
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:52.160
Yuya!

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:57.980
As you can see, there are no 
monsters or set cards on my field.

00:15:57.980 --> 00:16:03.240
My next draw will be the draw of 
destiny with everything on the line!

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:05.880
Make sure to applaud if I'm successful!

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:11.760
I draw!

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:15.690
It's here!

00:16:15.850 --> 00:16:19.660
I'll show you the strangest 
magic in the world!

00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:23.630
I can activate this card when 
there are no cards on my field,

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:26.270
and this is the only card in my hand!

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:29.500
The spell card Magician Manipulation!

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:35.940
I draw a card for every card on my 
opponent's field, and I reveal those cards.

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:39.480
Mr. Sawatari currently has 
five cards on his field.

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:42.160
Therefore, I draw five cards!

00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:48.400
I drew Skeeter Skimmer, Trump 
Witch, Timegazer Magician,

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:51.960
Turn Toad and Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:16:53.690 --> 00:16:55.930
He drew Odd-Eyes!

00:16:56.150 --> 00:16:58.400
Go, Yuya!

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:06.160
I set the Pendulum Scale with Scale 4 
Performapal Trump Witch and Scale 8 Timegazer Magician!

00:17:12.520 --> 00:17:16.320
It's Sakaki's authentic Pendulum Summon!

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:19.220
What kind of show will he display?

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:23.560
Now I can summon monsters between 
Level 5 and 7 simultaneously!

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:26.530
Swing, my soul's pendulum!

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:29.240
Draw an arc of light in the sky!

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:31.300
Pendulum Summon!

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:33.950
Come out, my monsters!

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:39.440
First is Performapal Drummerilla!

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:42.940
And the heroic one with beautiful 
different-colored eyes!

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:45.460
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:52.550
Both players are facing each 
other with their ace monsters!

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:54.680
It's time to finish this!

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:56.460
Yeah!  Let's battle!

00:17:56.460 --> 00:18:00.160
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon attacks Daibak!

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:02.860
It doesn't have enough attack points!

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:05.460
Drummerilla's effect activates!

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:11.740
When a monster battles, it gains 600 
attack points until the end of battle!

00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:16.520
Odd-Eyes's effect!

00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:19.980
When it battles a Level 5-or-above 
monster, battle damage is doubled!

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:22.200
Yosenju Shinchu L's effect!

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:26.350
When a Yosenju is destroyed, 
this card is destroyed instead!

00:18:27.680 --> 00:18:32.730
Sawatari stopped his ace 
monster from being destroyed!

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:35.080
I'm getting really excited!

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:37.200
I don't care who wins anymore!

00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:39.160
I want both of them to win!

00:18:39.160 --> 00:18:41.400
Yeah!  Do your best, you two!

00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:44.240
Let's enjoy ourselves!

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:47.320
Yeah!  The fun is only getting started!

00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:51.110
Performapal Trump Witch's 
Pendulum effect activates!

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:56.730
Once per turn, it can Fusion Summon with 
a monster on my field during battle!

00:18:56.730 --> 00:18:58.120
What?

00:18:58.120 --> 00:18:59.660
Fusion Summon?

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:00.920
During battle?

00:19:00.920 --> 00:19:02.450
That's possible?

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:08.370
The forest sage that thumps its chest,

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:12.880
become one with the mysterious dragon 
to give birth to a new power!

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:15.420
Fusion Summon!

00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:19.470
Come out, the ferocious dragon 
with glowing beastly eyes!

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:22.140
Beast-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:28.780
He Fusion Summoned using Pendulum Monsters!

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:34.250
You've already evolved a lot, Yuya Sakaki.

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:38.620
These great rivals both have 
monsters with 3000 attack points!

00:19:40.230 --> 00:19:44.980
Let's battle!  Beast-Eyes 
Pendulum Dragon attacks Daibak!

00:19:48.740 --> 00:19:51.170
They're both going for Action Cards!

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:09.720
I activate the Action Spell Burning Barrel!

00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:17.420
This card deals you damage equal to half the 
attack points of your destroyed monster!

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:20.360
Yuya!

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:27.420
What?

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:30.900
Sakaki changed the damaging 
flames into fireworks!

00:20:30.900 --> 00:20:32.200
It's beautiful.

00:20:33.300 --> 00:20:34.830
Wow!

00:20:35.820 --> 00:20:40.030
Due to the Action Spell Miracle, 
Beast-Eyes wasn't destroyed,

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:42.050
so your effect was negated!

00:20:42.440 --> 00:20:44.840
That was too splashy!

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:49.460
Beast-Eyes Pendulum 
Dragon's effect activates!

00:20:49.460 --> 00:20:51.780
When it destroys a monster in battle...

00:20:51.780 --> 00:20:54.200
...you take damage equal to the attack points

00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:57.270
of the Beast-Type monster that 
was used to Fusion Summon it!

00:20:57.480 --> 00:21:00.510
Drummerilla has 1600 attack points!

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:12.590
It's over!  The winner of the 
second match is Yuya Sakaki!

00:21:12.840 --> 00:21:15.050
He did it!

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:26.280
Sawatari?

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:36.960
We made them excited!

00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:43.780
I'll take you on anytime.

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:47.520
Yeah!  I'm looking forward to it!

00:21:48.020 --> 00:21:52.200
Yeah, this was the duel 
that I was yearning for.

00:21:52.460 --> 00:21:57.260
Dad, I think I've gotten a 
little closer to your level.

00:21:59.880 --> 00:22:03.040
Retrieve Sawatari's Pendulum Cards.

00:22:03.040 --> 00:22:05.880
Analyze them so that we can 
mass produce them quickly.

00:22:05.880 --> 00:22:07.160
Understood.

00:22:30.210 --> 00:22:34.850
As long as there's a smile

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:41.620
I'll risk my ultimate pride

00:22:44.050 --> 00:22:46.930
I always believe

00:22:47.090 --> 00:22:50.440
In my tomorrow

00:22:50.790 --> 00:22:56.040
With courageous wings
Just fly away!

00:22:59.340 --> 00:23:04.710
This duel of the soul 
(Break through the darkness with the miracle card!)

00:23:04.710 --> 00:23:11.560
A battle that surpasses clashing dimensions 
(The fun is only getting started!)

00:23:11.750 --> 00:23:18.260
For everyone to acquire their own dreams

00:23:18.790 --> 00:23:22.330
We go towards the mightiest future

00:23:48.540 --> 00:23:51.560
Sora's first opponent is Syun Kurosaki.

00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:56.120
He dealt real shockwaves in 
a regular duel on the street.

00:23:56.120 --> 00:24:00.780
Why is the culprit who attacked 
LDS in the Championship?

00:24:00.790 --> 00:24:03.920
Sora, be careful!  Don't let your guard down!

00:24:03.920 --> 00:24:05.890
Don't worry!

00:24:05.890 --> 00:24:09.320
I'm the one who's going to 
entertain the crowd this time!

00:24:09.600 --> 00:24:13.740
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V:
Neo Heartland City

00:24:13.740 --> 00:24:16.280
The fun is only getting started!
